explanation:
**Question type:** Drude model; relaxation time from conductivity.

**Given:** (n=8.5\times10^{28},\text{m}^{-3}),
(\sigma=6\times10^7,\Omega^{-1}\text{m}\^{-1}),
(m_e=9.1\times10\^{-31},\text{kg}),
(e=1.6\times10\^{-19},\text{C}).

\[ \sigma=\frac{ne^2\tau}{m_e}
\quad\Rightarrow\quad \tau=\frac{\sigma m_e}{ne^2}
\]

\[ \tau=\frac{(6\times10^7)(9.1\times10^{-31})}
{(8.5\times10^{28})(1.6\times10^{-19})\^2}
\approx2.50\times10\^{-14},\text{s} \]

